`ifndef HISI_VICAP_RDL
`define HISI_VICAP_RDL

regfile eHISI_VICAP_CH {
    name = "HiSilicon VICAP port/channel registers";
    desc = "
    One VICAP port/channel register group (`CH[16]` at 0x10000 + n x 0x2000). Offsets are rebased to the start of the group (the data sheet lists the registers of PORT 0 / CH 0 as 0x10000.. and 0x10300..; Figure 11-17 shows PORTn registers at 0x10000 + n x 0x4000 and CHn registers at 0x10300 + n x 0x2000). The PT_* registers (offsets 0x000..0x044) exist only in channels 0 and 4 (at most two external ports are supported; port 0 serves channels 0-3, port 1 channels 4-7); they are present but not implemented in the other groups. The Hi3520D has 8 channels (Hi3515A: 4), the data sheet space allocation shows 16.

    VENDOR CROSS-CHECK (docs/rdl-campaign/vicap-vendor.md; Source: vendor module hi3520D_viu.ko (Hi3520D_MPP_V2.0.5.1, HiMPP kernel module from the OpenIPC Hi3520D rootfs; static disassembly)): the vendor HAL addresses port p at base + 0x10000 + p x 0x8000 (VIU_HAL_SetPortEn and all PT accessors: index (p + 2) shifted left by 15) and channel c at base + 0x10300 + (c & 3) x 0x2000 + (c >> 2) x 0x8000 (VIU_HAL_GetChnReg: switch on c & 3 selects +0x0/0x2000/0x4000/0x6000, c >> 2 is shifted left by 15). Therefore the PT_* registers of the two Hi3520D ports sit in channel groups 0 and 4 (0x10000 and 0x18000, 0x8000 apart); the 0x4000 port spacing of the data sheet Figure 11-17 does not apply (previously: PORTn at 0x10000 + n x 0x4000 quoted from the figure). Offsets inside a group equal vendor offset + 0x300 for registers the vendor reaches through GetChnReg (vendor +0x100 = CH_CTRL 0x400, +0x110 = CH_CROP_START 0x410, +0x200 = CH_DITHER_CFG 0x500, +0x400 = CH_MSC_CFG 0x700, +0x500 = CH_VCDS_CFG 0x800, +0x640 = CH_LHFIR_SPH 0x940, +0x900 = CH_SUM_Y 0xC00). Confidence HIGH. Not verified on hardware.
    Board facts (2026-11-10, Linux driver test): channel group registers read 0 and drop writes until the port enable bit (PT_INTF_MOD.port_en) is set; the vendor HAL likewise enables the port first (VIU_DRV_EnableDev -> VIU_HAL_SetPortEn, then udelay of g_u32DelayTime = 100 us) and only afterwards programs channels.
    Global per-register source and confidence lines were added 2026-11-10 (user rule): 'Source: data sheet' text is unchanged data-sheet content; every 'Source: vendor module ...' line is derived from the proprietary module by static analysis and is not a data-sheet fact.
    ";

    reg {
        name = "Port mode register";
        desc = "PT_INTF_MOD is a port mode register.

Source: data sheet 11.1.6 PT_INTF_MOD (offset 0x10000, printed page 11-21, `datasheet.txt` line 33933).

Source: vendor module hi3520D_viu.ko (Hi3520D_MPP_V2.0.5.1, HiMPP kernel module from the OpenIPC Hi3520D rootfs; static disassembly), VIU_DRV_SetDevAttrByChip (0x13754), VIU_HAL_SetPortEn/ClkMode/WorkMode/InputMode/CompMode/FixCode, VIU_HAL_SetAdChnId/SetAdChnIdEn, confidence HIGH for the bit positions written: bit0 port_en (SetPortEn), bit1 clk_mode (SetPortClkMode; vendor always writes 0 for BT.656), [4:3] port_mod (SetPortCompMode; written by SetDataLayout only for the 16-bit/digital-camera modes), bit7 fix_code (SetPortFixCode; 0 unless BT.601 or digital camera input), [9:8] written by SetPortWorkMode with the multiplex count (0 = 1Mux, 1 = 2Mux, 2 = 4Mux; forced to 1 for BT1120 interleaved), [11:10] written by SetPortInputMode with the interface type (VI interface enum 0 BT656 -> 0, 1 BT601 -> 1, 2 -> 2, 3 BT1120 standard -> 0, 4 BT1120 interleaved -> 3), [13:12]/[15:14]/[17:16]/[19:18] channel IDs ch0..3 (SetAdChnId) and bits 20..23 id enables (SetAdChnIdEn, only when more than one way is multiplexed). NOTE: the vendor labels of [9:8] (multiplex count) and [11:10] (input interface type) are the reverse of the data-sheet field names port_mux_mode [9:8] / port_cap_mode [11:10] below (the data sheet names [11:10] as the 1/2/4-channel multiplexing field); for the 1-channel BT.656 case both fields are 0 so it does not matter there. Previously the data-sheet naming only. Vendor write order for a BT.656 device: CRG11 sc_sel and divider, channel clock on, 100 us, device reset released, WK_MODE ptN_mode, PT ch IDs, clk_mode 0, [9:8], [11:10], fix_code, then port_en LAST (VIU_DRV_EnableDev), 100 us. Not verified on hardware.";

        enum PT_INTF_MOD_interleave_seq_enum {
            C_COMPONENT_BEFORE = 0 { name = "C Component Before"; desc = "The C component is before the Y component."; };
            Y_COMPONENT_BEFORE = 1 { name = "Y Component Before"; desc = "The Y component is before the C component."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "interleave_seq";
            desc = "Y/C sequence during interleaving.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PT_INTF_MOD_interleave_seq_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } interleave_seq[24:24];

        enum PT_INTF_MOD_ch3_id_en_enum {
            CHANNEL_ID_NOT = 0 { name = "Channel Id Not"; desc = "The channel ID is not checked."; };
            DATA_CHANNEL_SELECTED = 1 { name = "Data Channel Selected"; desc = "The data channel is selected based on the channel ID."; };
        };

        field {
            name = "ch3_id_en";
            desc = "Channel 3 ID enable.";
