    reg {
        name = "Port test configuration register";
        desc = "PT_TEST_CFG is a port test configuration register.

Source: data sheet 11.1.6 PT_TEST_CFG (offset 0x10040, printed page 11-25, `datasheet.txt` line 34169).

Source: vendor module hi3520D_viu.ko (Hi3520D_MPP_V2.0.5.1, HiMPP kernel module from the OpenIPC Hi3520D rootfs; static disassembly), VIU_HAL_SetColorBarEn (0x13e38), confidence HIGH that bit 0 is a color bar enable at port base + 0x40: the HAL does read-modify-write of bit 0 only (cbar_en) at base + 0x10040 + port x 0x8000. The function is NOT called anywhere in hi3520D_viu.ko (no caller or exported use; the module has no test-pattern parameter or ioctl), and the vendor never writes hsync_sel [1] or interlace [2]; no timing or clock registers for the generator exist in the vendor code. The only related board script content (crgctrl_*_hi3520D.sh, 0x2003002C values 0x5524ff02 / 0x00241102 / 0xaa240102 / 0x0524f102) never sets PERI_CRG11.vi_selftest. Conclusion: the generator is probably a verification feature (the module also contains an empty RTL_Verify_RegWrite stub); whether it works in silicon is UNKNOWN. Not verified on hardware. Board 2026-11-10: with cbar_en (and hsync_sel/interlace variants) plus vi_selftest set, no frame start interrupt and IPI size 0 were observed.";

