    reg {
        name = "Port timing register 0";
        desc = "CH_INTF_CFG0 is timing register 0.

Source: data sheet 11.1.6 CH_INTF_CFG0 (offset 0x10300, printed page 11-27, `datasheet.txt` line 34256).

Source: vendor module hi3520D_viu.ko (Hi3520D_MPP_V2.0.5.1, HiMPP kernel module from the OpenIPC Hi3520D rootfs; static disassembly), VIU_HAL_SetChnInputMode ([6:5]), VIU_HAL_SetChnScanMode / SetChnCombineMode ([8:7]), VIU_HAL_SetChnSync, confidence HIGH for positions: [6:5] port_mode: the vendor writes the interface type (0 for BT.656 and BT.1120 standard, 1 and 2 for the sync-based BT.601/digital camera modes, 3 for BT.1120 interleaved; VIU_DRV_SetChnIntfCfg), [8:7] scan mode (bit7 = progressive when set, ScanMode(0 interlaced) clears bit7 and keeps bit8; CombineMode != 0 sets bit8 = Y/C separate). UNDOCUMENTED BITS found: VIU_HAL_SetChnSync writes six single bits of this register from the VI sync configuration (bits 4, 3, 2, 1, 9, 10: arguments in call order; HiMPP VI_SYNC_CFG_S members vsync field/pulse, vsync polarity, vsync valid and its polarity, hsync polarity), used only for BT.601 / digital camera input (not for BT.656; VIU_DRV_SetChnIntfCfg calls it only when the interface type is 1 or 2). Names and polarities are UNKNOWN, confidence LOW for the meaning (HIGH for the positions). Not verified on hardware.";

