        desc = "CH_INTF_CFG1 is timing register 1.

Source: data sheet 11.1.6 CH_INTF_CFG1 (offset 0x10304, printed page 11-28, `datasheet.txt` line 34314).

Source: vendor module hi3520D_viu.ko (Hi3520D_MPP_V2.0.5.1, HiMPP kernel module from the OpenIPC Hi3520D rootfs; static disassembly), VIU_HAL_SetChnYUVInputSeq ([5:4]), SetChnCompMode ([15:14]), SetChnFtcPolar (bit2), SetChnFixcode (bit3), SetChnCorrectEn (bit0), confidence HIGH for the positions. Vendor default path for BT.656 (VIU_DRV_SetChnIntfCfg, interface type 0): sav_ver_en = 0, ftc_cfg = 0, ftc_polar = 0, yuv_seq = 0 (UYVY; 1 for the other interface types), port_mod = 0. The Linux driver writes the whole register as 0, which is identical. Not verified on hardware.";

